{"lang": "", "lang_probs": [], "emotion": "", "event": "", "text": "The undertaking, which seemed so attractive when viewed as a literary task, proved a most difficult one, and at times became oppressive.", "timestamps": [], "durations": [], "tokens":["The", " undertaking", ",", " which", " seemed", " so", " attractive", " when", " viewed", " as", " a", " literary", " task", ",", " proved", " a", " most", " difficult", " one", ",", " and", " at", " times", " became", " oppressive", "."], "ys_log_probs": [], "words": []}
{"lang": "", "lang_probs": [], "emotion": "", "event": "", "text": "When I was a young man, I thought Paul was making too much of his call.", "timestamps": [], "durations": [], "tokens":["When", " I", " was", " a", " young", " man", ",", " I", " thought", " Paul", " was", " making", " too", " much", " of", " his", " call", "."], "ys_log_probs": [], "words": []}
{"lang": "", "lang_probs": [], "emotion": "", "event": "", "text": "Not gold or silver or pashal lambs or an angel, but himself. What for?", "timestamps": [], "durations": [], "tokens":["Not", " gold", " or", " silver", " or", " p", "ash", "al", " lam", "bs", " or", " an", " angel", ",", " but", " himself", ".", " What", " for", "?"], "ys_log_probs": [], "words": []}
{"lang": "", "lang_probs": [], "emotion": "", "event": "", "text": "This sentence also defines our sins as great, so great in fact that the whole world could not make amends for a single sin.", "timestamps": [], "durations": [], "tokens":["This", " sentence", " also", " defines", " our", " sins", " as", " great", ",", " so", " great", " in", " fact", " that", " the", " whole", " world", " could", " not", " make", " am", "ends", " for", " a", " single", " sin", "."], "ys_log_probs": [], "words": []}
{"lang": "", "lang_probs": [], "emotion": "", "event": "", "text": "This attitude springs from a false conception of sin: the conception that sin is a small matter, easily taken care of by good works; that we must present ourselves unto God with a good conscience; that we must feel no sin before we may feel that Christ was given for our sins.", "timestamps": [], "durations": [], "tokens":["This", " attitude", " springs", " from", " a", " false", " conception", " of", " sin", ":", " the", " conception", " that", " sin", " is", " a", " small", " matter", ",", " easily", " taken", " care", " of", " by", " good", " works", ";", " that", " we", " must", " present", " ourselves", " unto", " God", " with", " a", " good", " conscience", ";", " that", " we", " must", " feel", " no", " sin", " before", " we", " may", " feel", " that", " Christ", " was", " given", " for", " our", " sins", "."], "ys_log_probs": [], "words": []}
{"lang": "", "lang_probs": [], "emotion": "", "event": "", "text": "But they have nothing to do with the interpretation of Plato, and in spirit they are opposed to him.", "timestamps": [], "durations": [], "tokens":["But", " they", " have", " nothing", " to", " do", " with", " the", " interpretation", " of", " Plato", ",", " and", " in", " spirit", " they", " are", " opposed", " to", " him", "."], "ys_log_probs": [], "words": []}
{"lang": "", "lang_probs": [], "emotion": "", "event": "", "text": "There is a want of flow, and often a defect of rhythm. The meaning is sometimes obscure, and there is a greater use of apposition and more of repetition than occurs in Plato's earlier writings.", "timestamps": [], "durations": [], "tokens":["There", " is", " a", " want", " of", " flow", ",", " and", " often", " a", " defect", " of", " rhythm", ".", " The", " meaning", " is", " sometimes", " obscure", ",", " and", " there", " is", " a", " greater", " use", " of", " app", "osition", " and", " more", " of", " repetition", " than", " occurs", " in", " Plato", "'s", " earlier", " writings", "."], "ys_log_probs": [], "words": []}
{"lang": "", "lang_probs": [], "emotion": "", "event": "", "text": "And therefore, to you I turn, Timmias, citizen of Locrus, who are at once a philosopher and a statesman, and to you Critias, whom all Athenians know to be similarly accomplished, and to Hermocrates, who is also fitted by nature and education to share in our discourse.", "timestamps": [], "durations": [], "tokens":["And", " therefore", ",", " to", " you", " I", " turn", ",", " Tim", "m", "ias", ",", " citizen", " of", " Loc", "rus", ",", " who", " are", " at", " once", " a", " philosopher", " and", " a", " states", "man", ",", " and", " to", " you", " Crit", "ias", ",", " whom", " all", " Athen", "ians", " know", " to", " be", " similarly", " accomplished", ",", " and", " to", " Herm", "ocrates", ",", " who", " is", " also", " fitted", " by", " nature", " and", " education", " to", " share", " in", " our", " discourse", "."], "ys_log_probs": [], "words": []}
{"lang": "", "lang_probs": [], "emotion": "", "event": "", "text": "Some poems of Sullen were recited by the boys.", "timestamps": [], "durations": [], "tokens":["Some", " poems", " of", " S", "ullen", " were", " rec", "ited", " by", " the", " boys", "."], "ys_log_probs": [], "words": []}
{"lang": "", "lang_probs": [], "emotion": "", "event": "", "text": "Observe again what care the lot took in the pursuit of wisdom, searching out the deep things of the world, and applying them to the use of men.", "timestamps": [], "durations": [], "tokens":["Ob", "serve", " again", " what", " care", " the", " lot", " took", " in", " the", " pursuit", " of", " wisdom", ",", " searching", " out", " the", " deep", " things", " of", " the", " world", ",", " and", " applying", " them", " to", " the", " use", " of", " men", "."], "ys_log_probs": [], "words": []}
